//! Endianness declaration.
//!
//! `Endian` is the byte order of multi-byte values -- both instruction fields
//! (where applicable) and data-side memory loads/stores. ISAs whose
//! instruction encoding is a positional byte stream (e.g. COR24) and have
//! no multi-byte instruction fields simply set this to whatever the
//! *data-side* uses; instruction decoding for such ISAs ignores it.
//!
//! If a future ISA needs to distinguish "no multi-byte instruction fields"
//! from "multi-byte fields with explicit endianness", introduce that
//! distinction at the format level, not here. This enum is for byte order,
//! not for instruction-encoding layout.

#[derive(Copy, Clone, Debug, Eq, PartialEq)]
pub enum Endian {
    Big,
    Little,
}

